<title>USA: Commonwealth Edison gets $50,000 fine.</title>
<headline>Commonwealth Edison gets $50,000 fine.</headline>
<dateline>LISLE, Ill. 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Nuclear Regulatory Commission said it had fined Unicom Corp's Commonwealth Edison Co $50,000 for violations with its Zion Nuclear Power Station's transportation program for radioactive materials.</p>
<p>NRC said an inspection in December and January turned up four violations in Commonwealth Edison's radiation protection and transportation programs.</p>
<p>The utility has until July 17 to pay the fine or protest it, the NRC said.</p>
<p>((--Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
